handle_privacy() assigned cfg->privacy.save_state directly, so the value was
never tracked and never reached the user layer: enabling "remember runtime
state" from the web UI lasted only until the next restart.

The privacy section is reachable from the plain socket, from the runtime
transport and from the HTTP API, and its keys must persist from all three.
Add CFG::persist_paths() to write an explicit set of paths regardless of dirty
staging, and use it for save_state. Persisting the whole dirty set here would
also commit unrelated page edits that were still waiting for their own save.

